-- title:
--   Groups with n-torsion (ℤ/n)² have ψ(n) cyclic subgroups of order n
-- statement:
--   Let $n$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero, and let $A$ be an additive commutative group. Suppose given an isomorphism $e$ of additive groups from $\mathbb Z/n \times \mathbb Z/n$ onto `Submodule.torsionBy ℤ A n`, the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $A$ consisting of those $x$ with $n \cdot x = 0$, i.e. the $n$-torsion subgroup $A[n]$. Then the cardinality (in the sense of `Nat.card`) of the type of subgroups $H \le A$ satisfying both `IsAddCyclic H`, i.e. $H$ is generated by a single element, and $\operatorname{card} H = n$, equals [`ModularCurve.dedekindPsi n`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L201), which is by definition the sum $\sum_{d \mid n,\ d \text{ squarefree}} n/d$; this is the Dedekind value $\psi(n) = n\prod_{p \mid n}(1 + 1/p)$. In particular the assertion includes that there are only finitely many such subgroups, since otherwise the left-hand side would be $0$ while $\psi(n) \ge 1$.
--
--   This is the group-theoretic count underlying the fact that an elliptic curve whose $n$-torsion is full has exactly $\psi(n)$ cyclic subgroups of order $n$, i.e. $\psi(n) = \deg$ of the degeneracy data counting cyclic $n$-isogenies, and hence the number of points of $X_0(n)$ above a given $j$-invariant in the generic situation. It is used in the project's work on modular curves and modular polynomials, for instance in the analysis of fibres of the modular polynomial and in supersingular point counts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AddCommGroup_natCard_isAddCyclic_addSubgroup_eq_dedekindPsi_of_addEquiv_torsionBy.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X0

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point

theorem AddCommGroup.natCard_isAddCyclic_addSubgroup_eq_dedekindPsi_of_addEquiv_torsionBy
    (n : ℕ) [NeZero n] {A : Type*} [AddCommGroup A]
    (e : ZMod n × ZMod n ≃+ Submodule.torsionBy ℤ A n) :
    Nat.card {H : AddSubgroup A // IsAddCyclic H ∧ Nat.card H = n} = ModularCurve.dedekindPsi n := by sorry
